--- !u!114 &4889491062344484846
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4889491062344484832}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c63b78caf1e619144bf18b88688e4a91, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  spline: {fileID: 4889491062344484835}
  tourStops:
  - animationEndTime: 0
    splineEndTime: 0
    text: 
    selectableConstituentTypes: 
    annotation: []
    highlight: []
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 0
        Data2: 0
        Data3: 0
        Data4: 0
      Path: 
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 7.87
    splineEndTime: 0.1
    text: GLP-1 is a hormone that is released by the small intestine after eating.
      It travels through the bloodstream until it reaches its target, the GLP-1 receptor,
      GLP-1R, located on the membrane that surrounds the pancreatic beta cell.
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0500000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 838400649
        Data2: 1152791153
        Data3: -1877677392
        Data4: -939821874
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_01
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 10.3
    splineEndTime: 0.2
    text: 'GLP-1 fits into a binding pocket on GLP-1R. The binding pocket is composed
      of several amino acids whose overall shape accommodates the GLP-1. Drugs designed
      to treat diabetes mimic this interaction between GLP-1 and the binding pocket. '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0500000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight: []
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: -1267966398
        Data2: 1311053540
        Data3: -51899732
        Data4: -929943352
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_02
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 10.3
    splineEndTime: 0.21400058
    text: 'Proteins are composed of Amino Acids Amino acids on both the GLP-1 and
      the GLP-1R interact to keep the two proteins bound. Here you can see these
      amino acids highlighted. '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0500000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight: []
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 1863275755
        Data2: 1083338497
        Data3: 262192548
        Data4: 1070353208
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_03
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 12
    splineEndTime: 0.33700082
    text: "When GLP-1 and GLP-1R bind, there are two conformational changes in the
      GLP-1R. The first is a tilt of the extracellular domain, the second conformational
      change is a kink or bend in one of GLP-1R\u2019s helices."
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0500000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: -610750386
        Data2: 1217847133
        Data3: -1244307272
        Data4: -366966044
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_04
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 17.66
    splineEndTime: 0.41200113
    text: 'This change is important because it creates a second binding pocket.  '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 050000000600000007000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 248746673
        Data2: 1214468763
        Data3: -433062246
        Data4: -551528891
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_05
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 23.72
    splineEndTime: 0.4340022
    text: 'When G Proteins are bound to guanosine diphosphate (GDP) they are inactive.
      When the G Protein complex interacts with GLP-1R, the GDP is swapped for guanosine
      triphosphate (GTP). This activates the G Protein complex.  '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 07000000090000000a00000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: -1449878367
        Data2: 1215923543
        Data3: -1923195249
        Data4: 1386147889
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_06
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 26
    splineEndTime: 0.71999973
    text: "The activation of the G Protein complex allows it to split into two subunits,
      G\u03B2\u0263 and G\u03B1. "
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0700000008000000090000000a00000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 1053011344
        Data2: 1145622830
        Data3: -558992764
        Data4: 243921714
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_07
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 28.65
    splineEndTime: 0.78300023
    text: "The G\u03B1 subunit holds the GTP molecule and will take it to proteins
      in the next step in the insulin secretion pathway."
    selectableConstituentTypes: 07000000080000000a0000000900000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 899957917
        Data2: 1333683579
        Data3: 267300274
        Data4: 975490870
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_08
    animationPlaySpeed: 1
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 69.9
    splineEndTime: 0.81800103
    text: 'As long as GLP-1 remains bound to GLP-1R, it provides a window of opportunity
      for other G Proteins to be activated. The process will repeat 3-5 times depending
      on availability of G Proteins.  '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 060000000700000008000000090000000a000000
    annotation: []
    highlight: []
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: -1391094672
        Data2: 1125006923
        Data3: -42665324
        Data4: 1448916459
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_09
    animationPlaySpeed: 3
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
  - animationEndTime: 83.85
    splineEndTime: 1
    text: 'GLP-1 eventually leaves GLP-1R. The whole cycle can start again, with
      another GLP-1 binding to the receptor.  '
    selectableConstituentTypes: 0500000006000000
    annotation:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    highlight:
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    - {fileID: 0}
    voiceOverEvent:
      Guid:
        Data1: 1137259874
        Data2: 1329413444
        Data3: 935066496
        Data4: 883785598
      Path: event:/Vo/stop_10
    animationPlaySpeed: 2
    visualFocus: {fileID: 0}
